{
  "id": "COMPOUND:25979 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "Excisusin C is implicated in the biological pathway leading to LAMA-84 through multiple independent routes. The first pathway connects Excisusin C to VMRC-LCP, which is then targeted by Neridienone A, ultimately leading to LAMA-84. The second pathway links Excisusin C directly to MOVP-3, which is also targeted by the same compound, and this pathway also leads to LAMA-84. Both pathways involve the same intermediate compound, (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol, which is a complex and structurally defined molecule. The shared target of this compound in both pathways suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the same molecular interaction. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Excisusin C and LAMA-84 through a shared biochemical pathway, with the compound acting as a common intermediate in the regulation of LAMA-84. The mechanisms are consistent, and the evidence is robust, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
